# `src/agent/templates/**/*.tpl` is every file this CLI writes, held
# byte-for-byte as it will be written. Two consequences, and both are here
# rather than anywhere else:
#
#   1. **Line endings are LF, always.** esbuild's `text` loader puts a `.tpl`
#      into the bundle exactly as the checkout has it, so a Windows clone that
#      normalised these to CRLF would ship a CLI that writes CRLF into every
#      generated project — where that project's own `prettier --check .` fails
#      on the first run. `text eol=lf` is what makes the working copy LF on
#      every platform.
#   2. **GitHub highlights the diff.** The extension is `.tpl` so that `tsc`,
#      eslint and `scripts/verify-package.mjs` leave these files alone; the
#      cost is that linguist cannot guess a language, and `linguist-language`
#      is what pays it back.
*.tpl text eol=lf

*.ts.tpl linguist-language=TypeScript
*.md.tpl linguist-language=Markdown
*.jsonc.tpl linguist-language=JSON-with-Comments
*.json.tpl linguist-language=JSON
*.js.tpl linguist-language=JavaScript
